Changes made to LOOPZE

Orbit Flow started from LOOPZE in September 2026. The changes are recorded in
the history of the repository above. In summary:

- runs as an Orbit OS app and registers its page with the Orbit OS Launcher;
- Modbus RTU runs over the Orbit OS UART API instead of opening serial devices;
- new nodes for the device's own hardware and services: GPIO, I2C, SPI, system
  metrics, device identity and mobile notifications;
- the file nodes are limited to the app's data folder;
- the embedded NATS server opens no network port by default;
- renamed to Orbit Flow.

Files that came from LOOPZE keep the copyright notice of Dennis Bleul. Files
written for Orbit Flow carry the copyright notice of Orbit OS. All of them are
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later.

